Redis server v=7.2.11 sha=d4c381df:0 malloc=jemalloc-5.3.0 bits=64 build=e3db856fd57ff434

# 79.2 — INCRBY delta Long.MIN_VALUE
$ redis-cli -p 31991 set k1 0 >/dev/null; redis-cli -p 31991 incrby k1 -9223372036854775808
-9223372036854775808                      <- representable result returned
$ redis-cli -p 31991 set k2 -5 >/dev/null; redis-cli -p 31991 incrby k2 -9223372036854775808
ERR increment or decrement would overflow
$ redis-cli -p 31991 get k2
-5                                         <- value untouched
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrby k2b -9223372036854775807
ERR increment or decrement would overflow

# 79.1 — INCRBYFLOAT precision / trailing zeros
$ redis-cli -p 31991 del f1 f2 f3 f4
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat f1 0.001   -> 0.001
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat f1 0.001   -> 0.002
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat f1 0.001   -> 0.003
$ redis-cli -p 31991 set f2 10.50 >/dev/null; redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat f2 0.1
10.6                                      <- no trailing zero, full precision
$ redis-cli -p 31991 set f3 0 >/dev/null; redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat f3 0.1
0.1

# 79.8 — numeric literal strictness
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrby p1 +5    -> ERR value is not an integer or out of range
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrby p1 05    -> ERR value is not an integer or out of range
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrby p1 -0    -> ERR value is not an integer or out of range
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat p2 1.5d      -> ERR value is not a valid float
$ redis-cli -p 31991 incrbyfloat p2 " 1.5 "   -> ERR value is not a valid float

# 79.9 / 79.10 — INFO section matching
$ redis-cli -p 31991 info SERVER | head -1   -> # Server   (case-insensitive, single section)
$ redis-cli -p 31991 info Server | head -1   -> # Server
$ redis-cli --raw -p 31991 info foo          -> (empty output — empty bulk, no sections)
$ redis-cli --raw -p 31991 info all | grep -c '^#'     -> 13
$ redis-cli --raw -p 31991 info everything | grep -c '^#' -> 13
$ redis-cli -p 31991 info server memory | head -2      -> # Server / # Memory (multi-section)

## 3. Velo-side expectations (from code inspection at reviewed commit f7c06ee2)

- INCRBY k -9223372036854775808, current=0  → IGroup.java:153 `-by` == Long.MIN_VALUE →
  DGroup.java:415-418 guard `longValue > Long.MAX_VALUE + by` (= -1) fires → ERR increment or
  decrement would overflow (Redis: returns the value).
- INCRBY k -9223372036854775808, current=-5 → guard does not fire →
  `longValue - by` wraps → stores +9223372036854775803 and replies with it (Redis: overflow error,
  value untouched).
- INCRBYFLOAT k 0.001 → DGroup.java:404-405 `setScale(2, HALF_UP)` on value and delta → 0.00 - (-0.00)
  = 0.00, stored and replied "0.00" via DoubleReply (DoubleReply.java:36 setScale(2).toPlainString()).
- ingest json value_fields=* → IGroup.java:352 `["*"]` + 358-366 subMap {"*": null} →
  value `{"*":null}` for every ingested key.
- ingest file_pattern=test* → IGroup.java:269 `file.getName().matches("test*")` — Java regex,
  `test1.json` does not match; `testt` does.
